⊘⊘⊘ THE BRIEF'S PREMISE IS BACKWARDS ON ITS FIRST TERM. Briefed as 'we allow
the alloc, allow a control, and refuse the free'. Measured, we REFUSE the
alloc; the GUEST's kernel allows it, builds the object locally and returns
NV_OK to userspace regardless. The triple is REFUSE / SERVE / REFUSE, and the
odd row is the CONTROL, not the free.

  run_w294cup2_qemu.log   AllocClassNotPermitted::Refused x3 id=0x0000402c,0x000083de
  run_w294cup2_qemu.log   control 0x83de0309 result 0x00000000 x1
  w294nvd_ce_r1.jsonl.zst i=366 ALLOC 0x83de -> NV_OK   i=422 FREE 0x5c000072 -> 0x56
  run_s51_..._probe.log   both halves in ONE boot: userspace NV_OK, kernel GspRmAlloc
                          failed hClass=0x000083de status=0x00000056

So 'serving' 0x83de0309 answered NV_OK for state nothing on our side holds --
an echo, not a service. w292's ARGUMENT survives untouched: the control writes
no hardware and RM's default is _ALL. What it could not ask -- because nothing
in capability.rs could -- is whether we hold the object.

MECHANISM
  control_owner_class(cmd) = cmd >> 16, RM's own encoding, which this module
  already depended on in its BinApi rule; naming it lets a CLASS question be
  asked of a CONTROL.
  CapabilityTable::control refuses any command whose owner class is denied,
  carrying the CLASS's name and reason -- placed ABOVE both blanket rules,
  which is the half that outlives this one id: RM_GSS_LEGACY_MASK is bit 15,
  half the command space of EVERY class, and passes commands with no table row
  at all. No allowlist edit could ever have revealed a leak there.

GATES
  no_control_is_admitted_on_a_denied_class -- every boundary x every denied
  class x the RESOLVED answer, plus two synthetic probes per class so the
  blanket rules are covered too.
  the_class_gate_names_a_deliberate_disagreement -- the KNOWN-POSITIVE: builds
  a deliberate class/control disagreement, asserts the predicate names exactly
  it, asserts the resolved answer flips, and asserts the SAME control row with
  the class row removed is Listed, so the refusal cannot be the fixture being
  unreachable for another reason.

Three existing ratchets fired on 0x83de0309 and each gets a written position
rather than a deletion. Counts: 163->162 controls, uniform -8 across the eight
boundaries (a class denial refuses a whole cmd>>16 family, so a non-uniform
delta would mean the gate resolved differently per boundary), Nvproxy 149->148,
denied controls and denied classes both UNCHANGED -- nothing was added to the
deny side, a contradiction was removed from the admit side.

⚠ THE CASE IS AN OWNER CALL and is NOT decided here: whether GT200_DEBUGGER
should be denied at all. docs/design/class_control_consistency.md names the
boundary admitting it would widen, and the evidence that every CUDA context
allocates it on real hardware. The lever is now ONE LINE.

